% Mutually recursive predicates under the Magic rewrite.  even and odd call
% each other with the first column bound, so the rewrite records one
% adornment for each and stops: memoizing adornments on the predicate and
% its bound columns is what keeps the rewritten program finite.  The queries
% bind each column in turn, and bind neither, which reads both predicates
% through their all-free adornments.

next(n0, n1).
next(n1, n2).
next(n2, n3).
next(n3, n4).
next(n4, n5).
next(m0, m1).

even(X, X) :- next(X, _).
even(X, Z) :- next(X, Y), odd(Y, Z).
odd(X, Z) :- next(X, Y), even(Y, Z).

even(n0, Y)?
odd(X, n4)?
even(n0, n4)?
odd(X, Y)?
